§ `Section 672.51(1) -- Definition of disposition information`

-- 672.51(1): in this section, disposition information means all or part of an assessment report submitted to the court or Review Board and any other written information before the court or Review Board about the accused that is relevant to making or reviewing a disposition.
-- Reading taken (fork F-DISPINFO): "that is relevant to making or reviewing a disposition" qualifies the second limb, "any other written information"; an assessment report submitted to the court or Review Board counts whole or in part.
-- src:13691 | 672.51 (1) In this section, disposition information means all or part of an assessment report submitted to the court or Review Board and any other written information before the court or Review Board about the accused that is relevant to making or reviewing a disposition.
@ref s 672.51(1); s 672.51(1)"disposition information" (src:13691)
GIVEN `it is all or part of an assessment report submitted to the court or Review Board` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is other written information before the court or Review Board about the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is relevant to making or reviewing a disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.51(1) disposition information` MEANS
    IF `it is all or part of an assessment report submitted to the court or Review Board` OR (`it is other written information before the court or Review Board about the accused` AND `it is relevant to making or reviewing a disposition`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "disposition information means all or part of an assessment report submitted to the court or Review Board"

§ `Section 672.51(2) to (12) -- Who may see disposition information`

-- 672.51(3): the court or Review Board shall withhold some or all of the disposition information from an accused where it is satisfied, on the basis of that information and the evidence or report of the medical practitioner responsible for the assessment or treatment of the accused,
-- that disclosure of the information would be likely to endanger the life or safety of another person or would seriously impair the treatment or recovery of the accused.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13695 | (3) The court or Review Board shall withhold some or all of the disposition information from an accused where it is satisfied, on the basis of that information and the evidence or report of the medical practitioner responsible for the assessment or treatment of the accused, that disclosure of the information would be likely to endanger the life or safety of another person or would seriously impair the treatment or recovery of the accused.
@ref s 672.51(3) (src:13695)
GIVEN `the court or Review Board is satisfied, on the basis of the information and the evidence or report of the medical practitioner responsible for the assessment or treatment of the accused, that disclosure would be likely to endanger the life or safety of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or Review Board is satisfied, on that basis, that disclosure would seriously impair the treatment or recovery of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.51(3) the court or Review Board must withhold disposition information from the accused` MEANS
    IF `the court or Review Board is satisfied, on the basis of the information and the evidence or report of the medical practitioner responsible for the assessment or treatment of the accused, that disclosure would be likely to endanger the life or safety of another person` OR `the court or Review Board is satisfied, on that basis, that disclosure would seriously impair the treatment or recovery of the accused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where it is satisfied, on the basis of that information and the evidence or report of the medical practitioner responsible for the assessment or treatment of the accused"

-- 672.51(4): notwithstanding (3), the court or Review Board may release some or all of the disposition information to an accused where the interests of justice make disclosure essential in its opinion.
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE
-- src:13697 | (4) Notwithstanding subsection (3), the court or Review Board may release some or all of the disposition information to an accused where the interests of justice make disclosure essential in its opinion.
@ref s 672.51(4) (src:13697)
GIVEN `the interests of justice make disclosure essential in the opinion of the court or Review Board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.51(4) the court or Review Board may release disposition information to the accused` MEANS
    IF `the interests of justice make disclosure essential in the opinion of the court or Review Board`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the interests of justice make disclosure essential in its opinion"

-- 672.51(5): the court or Review Board shall withhold disposition information from a party other than the accused or an Attorney General, where disclosure to that party, in the opinion of the court or Review Board, is not necessary to the proceeding and may be prejudicial to the accused.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13699 | (5) The court or Review Board shall withhold disposition information from a party other than the accused or an Attorney General, where disclosure to that party, in the opinion of the court or Review Board, is not necessary to the proceeding and may be prejudicial to the accused.
@ref s 672.51(5) (src:13699)
GIVEN `the party is other than the accused or an Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `disclosure to that party is not necessary to the proceeding, in the opinion of the court or Review Board` IS A BOOLEAN
      `disclosure to that party may be prejudicial to the accused, in the opinion of the court or Review Board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.51(5) the court or Review Board must withhold disposition information from the party` MEANS
    IF `the party is other than the accused or an Attorney General` AND `disclosure to that party is not necessary to the proceeding, in the opinion of the court or Review Board` AND `disclosure to that party may be prejudicial to the accused, in the opinion of the court or Review Board`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where disclosure to that party, in the opinion of the court or Review Board, is not necessary to the proceeding and may be prejudicial to the accused"

-- 672.51(2): subject to this section, all disposition information shall be made available for inspection by, and the court or Review Board shall provide a copy of it to, each party and any counsel representing the accused.
-- The two inputs are the answers of subsections (3) and (5): where either requires the information to be withheld from this person, subsection (2) yields.
-- fork: F-SUBJECT
-- src:13693 | (2) Subject to this section, all disposition information shall be made available for inspection by, and the court or Review Board shall provide a copy of it to, each party and any counsel representing the accused.
@ref s 672.51(2) (src:13693)
GIVEN `it is disposition information, by s 672.51(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a party or counsel representing the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information must be withheld from the person, by s 672.51(3) or (5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.51(2) disposition information must be made available for inspection by, and a copy provided to, the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`it is disposition information, by s 672.51(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all disposition information shall be made available"
        IF NOT `the person is a party or counsel representing the accused` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each party and any counsel representing the accused"
        IF `the information must be withheld from the person, by s 672.51(3) or (5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to this section"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 672.51(6): a court or Review Board that withholds disposition information from the accused or any other party pursuant to subsection (3) or (5) shall exclude the accused or the other party from the hearing during (a) the oral presentation of that disposition information;
-- or (b) the questioning by the court or Review Board or the cross-examination of any person concerning that disposition information.
