      `it is the questioning by the court or Review Board or the cross-examination of any person concerning that disposition information` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.51(6) the court or Review Board must exclude the person from the hearing` MEANS
    IF `the court or Review Board withholds disposition information from the person pursuant to subsection 672.51(3) or (5)` AND (`it is the oral presentation of that disposition information` OR `it is the questioning by the court or Review Board or the cross-examination of any person concerning that disposition information`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A court or Review Board that withholds disposition information from the accused or any other party pursuant to subsection (3) or (5) shall exclude the accused or the other party, as the case may be, from the hearing during"

-- 672.51(7): no disposition information shall be made available for inspection or disclosed to any person who is not a party to the proceedings (a) where the disposition information has been withheld from the accused or any other party pursuant to (3) or (5);
-- or (b) where the court or Review Board is of the opinion that disclosure would be seriously prejudicial to the accused and that, in the circumstances, protection of the accused takes precedence over the public interest in disclosure.
