      `the court or Review Board is of the opinion that disclosure would be seriously prejudicial to the accused and that, in the circumstances, protection of the accused takes precedence over the public interest in disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.51(7) the section bars disposition information from being made available to or disclosed to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is not a party to the proceedings` AND (`the disposition information has been withheld from the accused or any other party pursuant to subsection 672.51(3) or (5)` OR `the court or Review Board is of the opinion that disclosure would be seriously prejudicial to the accused and that, in the circumstances, protection of the accused takes precedence over the public interest in disclosure`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No disposition information shall be made available for inspection or disclosed to any person who is not a party to the proceedings (a) where the disposition information has been withheld"

-- 672.51(8): no part of the record of the proceedings in respect of which the accused was excluded pursuant to subparagraph 672.5(10)(b)(ii) or (iii) shall be made available for inspection to the accused or to any person who is not a party to the proceedings.
