§ `Sections 672.52 and 672.53 -- Record; irregularity`

-- 672.52(1): the court or Review Board shall cause a record of the proceedings of its disposition hearings to be kept, and include in the record any assessment report submitted.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13724 | 672.52 (1) The court or Review Board shall cause a record of the proceedings of its disposition hearings to be kept, and include in the record any assessment report submitted.
@ref s 672.52(1) (src:13724)
GIVEN `it is a disposition hearing of the court or Review Board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.52(1) the court or Review Board must cause a record of the proceedings to be kept` MEANS
    IF `it is a disposition hearing of the court or Review Board`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a record of the proceedings of its disposition hearings"

-- 672.52(2): if a court holds a disposition hearing under subsection 672.45(1), whether or not it makes a disposition, it shall send without delay to the Review Board that has jurisdiction in respect of the matter, in original or copied form, a transcript of the hearing, any other document or information related to the hearing,
-- and all exhibits filed with it, if the transcript, document, information or exhibits are in its possession.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13726 | (2) If a court holds a disposition hearing under subsection 672.45(1), whether or not it makes a disposition, it shall send without delay to the Review Board that has jurisdiction in respect of the matter, in original or copied form, a transcript of the hearing, any other document or information related to the hearing, and all exhibits filed with it, if the transcript, document, information or exhibits are in its possession.
@ref s 672.52(2) (src:13726)
GIVEN `a court holds a disposition hearing under subsection 672.45(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transcript, document, information or exhibits are in its possession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.52(2) the court must send the transcript, documents and exhibits to the Review Board without delay` MEANS
    IF `a court holds a disposition hearing under subsection 672.45(1)` AND `the transcript, document, information or exhibits are in its possession`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a court holds a disposition hearing under subsection 672.45(1), whether or not it makes a disposition"

-- 672.52(3): the court or Review Board shall state its reasons for making a disposition in the record of the proceedings, and shall provide every party with a copy of the disposition and those reasons.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13728 | (3) The court or Review Board shall state its reasons for making a disposition in the record of the proceedings, and shall provide every party with a copy of the disposition and those reasons.
