GIVEN `there is a procedural irregularity in relation to a disposition hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it causes the accused substantial prejudice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.53 the procedural irregularity affects the validity of the hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `there is a procedural irregularity in relation to a disposition hearing` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any procedural irregularity in relation to a disposition hearing"
        IF `it causes the accused substantial prejudice` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless it causes the accused substantial prejudice"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect the validity of the hearing unless it causes the accused substantial prejudice"
